Work, potential difference and reference choice (@em-potential: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/University-Physics-Volume-2.lingua#r_5JQ0CPQ0RNJNVH175Y9V305J5Q", #source "../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1", #electromagnetism "Conductors-electrostatic-equilibrium-and-shielding.lingua#r_137AR1F19ABQJW33AB60E4ANFD", #hephaestus-core "../../core/Connect-signed-current-to-accumulated-and-stored-charge.lingua#r_00A2CB2AB667C70FE4724DA940") { r_0KDY19PKDZXWKFN38GPNQMKR3N
**Read:** [University Physics Volume 2 — OpenStax](../sources/University-Physics-Volume-2.lingua#r_5JQ0CPQ0RNJNVH175Y9V305J5Q), chapter 7 in full; [Electromagnetism — David Tong](../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1), electrostatic work, potentials and energy.

In electrostatics E = −∇V and the work done by the field on charge q from a to b is q(V_a − V_b). Potential energy changes by q(V_b − V_a). A voltage is a difference; adding a constant to V leaves the field unchanged. A reference at infinity is useful for localized sources but may be unsuitable for infinite ideal distributions.

For a uniform field in the positive x direction, V decreases with x. A positive released charge gains kinetic energy while its electric potential energy falls. The same voltage difference changes a negative charge's potential energy with the opposite sign. Distinguish a conservative field from a time-varying induced field, where a single scalar voltage cannot describe every loop integral.

Derive potential integrals for point and continuous sources and recover the field by differentiation. Compare the ring's nonzero midpoint potential with its zero midpoint field. Trace a voltmeter's leads and reference path in a time-dependent magnetic environment; the reading can depend on the measurement loop. Later induction and gauge records explain exactly which part of the electrostatic account must be extended.

**Continue:** [Conductors, electrostatic equilibrium and shielding](Conductors-electrostatic-equilibrium-and-shielding.lingua#r_137AR1F19ABQJW33AB60E4ANFD).

**Return:** [Electromagnetism — charge, fields, matter, waves and physical evidence](../Electromagnetism.lingua#r_5TJPESCTTNAKY66JH2QNQYN1PY).

**Fifth physics-block reading:** Read the work/reference/sign account and compare it with the explicitly derived source-avoiding parametrized-path proof in the common lesson. General gradient notation, continuous distributions, induction/measurement-loop and gauge theory remain later preparation; the complete original readings and examples remain assigned.

**Continue in the fifth physics block:** [Connect signed current to accumulated and stored charge](../../core/Connect-signed-current-to-accumulated-and-stored-charge.lingua#r_00A2CB2AB667C70FE4724DA940).

